Health scores and missing observations
=====================================

Health scores are a weighted summary of available component scores, from 0 to
100. A measured zero means a failed measurement. Missing data has no numeric
score and is shown as N/A with unknown status. An empty site is not healthy.

Site, organization, module, ranking, WAN and SLA calculations exclude unknown
DeviceHealth records from score averages. The measured_device_count fields
identify the denominator for current aggregates; device_count counts health
records, including unknown records, not a complete discovery inventory. The
organization average weights sites by their measured records, not by unknown
records. Inspect coverage as well as the score.

Top Issues reports a worst component only when an actual component score is
present. Missing components are N/A, never a green "unknown: 100" badge. A real
100 remains a measured component, and a real zero remains critical. An older
aggregate row can retain its overall score while lacking component observations;
the API represents those two facts separately rather than inventing a cause.

The scheduled device calculation currently contributes online/offline status
and configuration drift only when a running configuration has been collected.
It clears unobserved components on each recomputation; it does not assume that
firmware is current or that error rates are zero. Partial reconciliation updates
may retain previously collected components. A high score can therefore reflect
only one available component. It does not certify firmware security, overall
device correctness, or full monitoring coverage.

Reachability scores are not availability percentages over time. These health
endpoints leave uptime_percent unavailable until a time-window availability
collector provides evidence. Rankings report unknown trend when either today's
score or a usable previous daily snapshot is missing. Missing daily values and
sparkline values remain gaps rather than zeroes.

Upgrade and historical limits
-----------------------------

No database migration or history deletion is required. The existing non-null
numeric database columns remain for compatibility. health_status=unknown makes
the stored device number unavailable through the API and aggregate queries.
Daily snapshot status counts likewise distinguish unmeasured snapshots.

The next scheduled recomputation corrects current managed-device rows. Existing
scores previously marked healthy cannot be retroactively certified: their
component provenance was not recorded. Existing historical records are retained
unchanged and may include older assumed values. Do not use that history as
independently verified SLA or security evidence.

These changes do not establish a freshness SLA for device status/configuration,
deduplicate physical observations, or implement missing firmware, latency,
utilization and error collectors. Review collection timestamps and monitoring
coverage before acting on a score. Full freshness/provenance qualification is a
separate release requirement.
